Project Planning Phase

ComicCraft-AI – Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

The Project Planning Phase is the stage where the objectives, requirements, resources, schedule, and development activities of the ComicCraft-AI project are planned. The main goal is to develop an AI-based application that can create comic stories using Gemini models.

1. Project Objective

The main objective of ComicCraft-AI is to create an easy-to-use AI application that helps users generate creative comic stories from simple ideas.

The system will:

Generate comic stories from user prompts.

Create characters and their descriptions.

Generate scenes and dialogues.

Divide the story into comic panels.

Allow users to edit and regenerate content.

Provide a preview of the completed comic.


2. Project Scope

The project will focus on developing a comic story creation system using Gemini AI.

Included:

User story input

Genre and character selection

AI story generation

Character generation

Scene and dialogue generation

Comic panel organization

Story editing

Save and export functionality


Not included in the initial version:

Professional animation production

Advanced video editing

Large-scale social networking features


3. Project Development Plan

Phase	Activities

1. Requirement Analysis	Identify user needs and system requirements
2. Project Planning	Define objectives, resources, schedule and risks
3. System Design	Design architecture, database and user interface
4. Development	Develop frontend, backend and Gemini integration
5. AI Integration	Connect Gemini models and create suitable prompts
6. Testing	Test functionality, AI output and user interface
7. Deployment	Deploy the application
8. Maintenance	Fix errors and improve features


4. Resource Planning

Hardware Requirements

Computer/laptop

Internet connection

Minimum 4 GB RAM

Modern web browser


Software Requirements

Visual Studio Code

HTML, CSS, JavaScript/React

Python or Node.js

Database such as Firebase/MongoDB

Gemini API

Git/GitHub


5. Team Planning

Possible team responsibilities:

Project Manager: Plans and monitors the project.

UI/UX Developer: Designs the application interface.

Frontend Developer: Develops user-facing screens.

Backend Developer: Develops server-side functionality.

AI Developer: Integrates Gemini models and designs prompts.

Tester: Tests the application and reports errors.


6. Project Schedule

Week	Task

Week 1	Requirement analysis
Week 2	Project planning and research
Week 3	System and UI design
Week 4–5	Frontend and backend development
Week 6	Gemini API integration
Week 7	Story and comic generation features
Week 8	Testing and debugging
Week 9	Final improvements
Week 10	Documentation and presentation


7. Risk Planning

Risk	Solution

Gemini API failure	Provide error handling and retry options
Poor AI-generated story	Improve prompts and allow regeneration
Internet failure	Show appropriate error messages
High API usage	Limit unnecessary API requests
Data loss	Use database storage and backups
Software bugs	Perform regular testing


8. Expected Outcome

At the end of the project, ComicCraft-AI will provide a simple platform where users can enter a basic story idea and receive an AI-generated comic story containing characters, scenes, dialogues, captions, and comic panels.

9. Project Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful if:

Users can easily enter a story idea.

Gemini successfully generates a structured comic story.

Characters and dialogues are generated correctly.

The story can be divided into comic panels.

Users can edit and regenerate content.

The application works reliably and provides a user-friendly experience.
